    {
      "text": "Horsea eats small insects and moss off of rocks. If the ocean current turns fast, this Pokémon anchors itself by wrapping its tail around rocks or coral to prevent being washed away.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "If Horsea senses danger, it will reflexively spray a dense black ink from its mouth and try to escape. This Pokémon swims by cleverly flapping the fin on its back.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it senses any danger, it will vigorously spray water or a special type of ink from its mouth.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it senses any danger, it will vigorously spray water or a special type of ink from its mouth.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Horsea makes its home in oceans with gentle currents. If this Pokémon is under attack, it spits out pitch-black ink and escapes.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "They swim with dance-like motions and cause whirlpools to form. Horsea compete to see which of them can generate the biggest whirlpool.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
